{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/435410-da-pillars-for-the-modern-day-traditions","id":435410,"title":"DA Pillars for the modern day Traditions.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-10T00:41:16-07:00","id":435410,"title":"DA Pillars for the modern day Traditions.","content":"Has anyone tried to use the Pillar system from DA: Mage for an Ascension chronicle?<br /> <br /> Would the Verbenae have the Old Faith Pillars and Foundation, Order of Hermes it's old Foundation and Pillars?<br /> How would the Magics of the Akashics, Euthanatos, Society of Ether etc look like?<br /> <br /> Or perhaps a simpler matter. Keep the Sphere system but help me impose limitations on the Spheres for the various Traditions, help bring out what the various traditions are good at/bad at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T03:59:19-07:00","id":435533,"title":"","content":"Pillars in the modern era are an interesting idea, but they run up against issues to do with modern paradigms being very loose. The Dark Ages mechanics have very strict paradigm limitations, because the setting has very strict paradigm limitations. That doesn't mean you can't do it, just that I find the Traditions as presented don't have a great deal of unity in their paradigms beyond the broadest outlines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or perhaps a simpler matter. Keep the Sphere system but help me impose limitations on the Spheres for the various Traditions, help bring out what the various traditions are good at/bad at. </div> </div> </div>I think you might be overcomplicating it. If you don't want a character to be good at something, don't give them the sphere levels. The Order of Hermes has a handful of master Forces users, and they're the Forces tradition.<br /> <br /> Also, remember that most Traditionalists are going to be played by the ST, so if you want the Order of Hermes to be unable to... I dunno... slow down time in combat. Then make it clear that though the players might find a way around that limitation, the NPCs can't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T07:11:50-07:00","id":435648,"title":"","content":"Not really Pillars, but we have discussed Specialty Spheres for Technocrats here on the forum that are more Pillar then Sphere.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2379B5\"><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/428316-the-machine-sphere/page2\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-sphere/page2</a></b></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T09:16:30-07:00","id":435811,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I was looking at the machine sphere and that got me thinking.<br /> <br /> The Pillars are very paradigm based and actually helps players to see how paradigm works there are tangible limitations on what kind of magic the various traditions are good/bad at. The sphere system to me screams that everyone is equally good at everything which isnt the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T09:36:59-07:00","id":435831,"title":"","content":"Michael has a point in that one of the themes of the modern Ascension setting is that the Traditions are (supposedly) striving for a degree of unity. Porthos' Ambassador program, the cross-Tradition cabals and factions in Guide to the Traditions etc. are examples of this in action. One of the benefits of the Sphere system is supposed to be that it helps one Tradition learn from the other. They don't have to be equally good at everything but a modern Pillars system should reflect this aptitude for cross-pollination in some way if it is to fit the standard Ascension setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T10:08:47-07:00","id":435874,"title":"","content":"There was a thread a bit ago about redesigning the Spheres. My idea was to basically add in 3 sub-Sphere level traits per Sphere (Ok it was bigger than that, but it's the part that matters to this) that allowed a bit more flavor/customization. The point of this was to keep the general Sphere structure and the cross-compatibility stuff, but have more Tradition/Splat flavor around. So a Verbena and an Etherite might have the same dots in Life, but the Verbena might have &quot;Healing, Shapeshifting, and Plant Mastery,&quot; to reflect how they relate to Life and what kind of spells they're good at, while the Etherite might have, &quot;Body Modification, Genetics, and Homeostatic Control.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> I guess some of this is rather than looking at &quot;limiting&quot; mages into their Tradition/Splat paradigms, doing more of a carrot to encourage them to play to the strengths of their paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T10:08:59-07:00","id":435875,"title":"","content":"I don't have a problem with the Traditions learning from each other. But in that cas it should be something like learning another traditions pillar/s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T11:03:19-07:00","id":435970,"title":"","content":"What if a mage wants to adopt certain techniques from another Tradition or paradigm, but doesn't want to learn an entire Pillar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T11:39:03-07:00","id":436009,"title":"","content":"I think the bigger issue is that the Traditions aren't Fellowships. They're collections of Fellowships relating to an overarching idea, which don't necessarily agree on very much beyond that. To do it justice you really need to give each sub-tradition it's own pillars, which is a hell of a lot of work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T17:14:58-07:00","id":436438,"title":"","content":"you might just keep the old pillars and expand them a bit.<br /> <br /> e.g anima ,vires,primus,corona,materia and a new temporis pillar for the order of hermes.<br /> <br /> i have copied some pilars that malcolm sheppard wrote for the chakravanti and akashics ill post them later for anyone interested<br /> this is for the akashics<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Foundation:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">In this period, we call the Foundation the Vajra (&quot;diamond&quot; or &quot;thunderbolt&quot;),</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">represented the dynamic potential of anlightenment. Some Tibetan Akashics will</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">call it Dralaphurba (&quot;windhorse-thunder&quot;) which will later be known as</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Draladhrama, the modern syncretic term. Their aura penalizes rolls which require</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">expressing intimacy.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Akashics have an aura of emptiness, like they are a vast, empty space that</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">consumes the unprepared.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Rank 1: Normal and supernatural Social rolls have a +1 difficulty due to the</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Akashic's subtle nature.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Rank 3: Attempts to alter the Akashic's mind with supernatural powers (Doiminate,</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Obligation, Crona, etc.) face a +1 difficulty penalty since the Akashic's mind</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">becomes consumed with esoteric symbols wrapped around an empty space.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Rank 5: The Akashic's body now obeys formless, esoteric patterns that are almost</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">unpredictable. Opponents now face a +1 difficulty penalty to strike with physical</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">attacks, unless they directly target the character's pattern.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Pillars:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">The four pillars are called &quot;kaya&quot; (&quot;bodies&quot;). These correspond to the different</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">paths to enlightenment and the different elemental symbols of reality.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">The Nirmanakaya is the Scarlet Phoenix-Body. This corresponds to the the physical</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">body, as well as practices based on everyday observance and society at large.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Many physical applications of Do sping from this Pillar. This Pillar is rigid and</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">emphasizes custom.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Rank 1: Sense the flow of propriety in a being or place; whether a person is</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">healthy, whether Quintessence flows naturally through a place (instaed of being</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">twisted or snagged) and whether a person is speaking honestly.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Rank 2: Can use proper medicine and exercise to heal oneself of bashing or lethal</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">damage, can smooth chi flow along its proper course (but not determine what that</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">course is; he can return strength to a Dragon Nest, but not add extra strength to</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">it) and can detect supernatural compulsion in others and ward it off in himself.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Rank 3: Learns proper rigid forms to increase physical prowess, medicine to heal</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">bashing and lethal in others and aggravated in himself. The Akashic can also ward</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">off supernatural compulsion in a person or area.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Rank 4: The Akashic can force people or spirits to obey any vow they willingly</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">make. He can heal aggravated wounds in others by using traditional medicine and</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">sustain his body with discipline so strong that it can ward off fire and shatter</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">swords and spears.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Rank 5: The Akashic is a disciplined master of external rigid power and internal</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">sensitivity to the structure of the Tapestry. He can enter Heaven (the Astral</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Umbra) at will and cannot be cut off from the universe, since he can use rites</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">and exercises to take chi from anywhere.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">The Sambhokaya is the Pearl Tiger-Body. It is the Pillar of communication and of</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">opening oneself to invisible realms. Akashic who deal with the gods make use of</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">this kaya.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Rank 1: The Akashic can peer into the Umbra and can improve his ability to</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">communicate (-1 difficulty/success), but not use telepathy or languages that he</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">does not know. He can see if active spirits are possessing people or places.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Rank 2: The Akashic can sense emotions and can engage in voluntarily telepathic</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">speech with others, including spirits on the other side of the Umbra.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Rank 3: The Akashic can telepathically communicate with anyone and can even</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">overcome resistance. He can enter dreams and send terrible visions (inflicting</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">bashing damage) to people or spirits. He can even reach into the Umbra while</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">staying in the normal world.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Rank 4: Communication with even slumbering spirits is possible, and the Akashic</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">can even speak to past incarnations of entities through the Akashic Record. The</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">mage can makes spirits visible and tangible to others, as well. All this</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">information allows him to avoid surprise and improve alertness with bonuses to</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">defensive dice pools.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Rank 5: Akashics can communicate with something to the extent that they become</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">that thing, animating a statue, rock, person or spirit, whether they like it or</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">not. The character can also speak directly to patterns allowing him to animate or</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">destroy them (aggravated, resisted by Willpower).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">The Dharmakaya is also called the Dragon-Body and represents the dissolution of</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">preconceived ideas. Akashic tap this with internal martial arts, quiet meditation</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">and austerity. The student leaves behind illusions to see things as they are,</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">leading to simple but powerful magic.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Rank 1: The Akashic can see through illusions, including mundane disguises and</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">magical deceptions, and even fients and distractions in combat (grants an</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">initiative bonus)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Rank 2: You would say that the Akashic could &quot;divide&quot; his mind, but really, the mind expands to encompass many things. A spell allows the character to fully concentrate on multiple nonmagical actions (1 for each arm in addition to one spell, usually). The Akashic can also let his sense of self dissolve, becoming silent or invisible.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Rank 3: The Akashic abandons egotism in movement and sees that time is arbitrary (allowing multiple actions) and sees the natural flaws in structure (allowing extra damage). He can also honestly judge the abilities of others (determining their traits with a spell, so long as the character could see them in action).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Rank 4: The character's sense of place is an illusion; he can teleport from place</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">to place and affect things from a distance.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">rank 5: The mage can now be many places at once and can provide minds for each</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">node of experience. He realizes all living chi belongs to a single, cosmic flow</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">and can siphon it to and from other creatures.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Swabhavakaya, the Windhorse-Body is the path of black magic and quick, brutal</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">esoteric training. It tranforms the Akashic into a living mystical symbol, able</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">to change other symbols and thus, the creatures attached to them. It includes</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">dangerous arts like karma manipulation.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Rank 1: By studying omens and meditative visions, the character can sense the odds of a future event and recognize mighty or infamous destinies.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Tahoma\">Blah, blah, blah. You guys do the rest.</span></span>.(seriously i think that's what he wrote<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","user":"mark","date":". 03-10-2015, 08:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T21:28:59-07:00","id":436653,"title":"","content":"Sphere system is excellent because it's one clear system that can be used in the background so to speak to represent all magic that is it gives us common mechanical ground to build upon while it is the individual Paradigms that limit and guide how the Spheres can be used. That is to say you should look at Spheres as framework of your magical might and the theoretical limits of what you would be able to do had you ascended Paradigms but always look at them trough the lens of your Paradigm you can only do things you can fit inside and explain through your Paradigm.<br /> <br /> Pillars are a fine method of enforcing Paradigmal thinking if your having trouble with it but essentially it is a crutch and you need one for each Paradigm out there, Orphans have their own unique and personal Pillars while each Craft, Tradition and even many intra-tradition factions have each their own though they may share aspects. This is the basic reason why the Sphere system is so brilliant it allows for all this with less work as you do not need to create a dozen or so unique Foundations and 30 or more individual Pillars to get an idea of general limits to the Character imposed by the system. It allows one system to represent all of the above with each player filling in the details on top of that common frame of reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T14:25:28-07:00","id":437533,"title":"","content":"Possessed: I think that you aren't taking the next step in the process. While the Sphere system is, of course, very good at creating a list of metaphysical concepts that can give various players/STs ideas that they may never have thought of, the system is still, itself, <i>just another paradigm</i>. This wouldn't be an issue if, say, the general setting was one of the numerous, default DnD settings, where few characters (and even fewer players) actually go that deep into questioning why/how magic works for them/their world -- they just accept it, by-and-large, and get about their business. That's almost antithetical in terms of Mage, where paradigm is stressed left, right and center, and much of the fluff of the narratives involved is about the characters coming to question not only Reality(tm), their own beliefs, and the beliefs of others, but also coming to understand how said beliefs have a direct influence on how Reality(tm) works (and, in an equal fashion, vice-versa). On that level, even the most simple of meta-game discussions reveal the fundamental truths (and flaws) of the Sphere system: *plenty* of players back in the 90's/00's (and today, still) ask &quot;why do I have to spend &quot;x&quot; points to get &quot;y&quot; up to &quot;z&quot; level, when in my character's paradigm, he only needs -- and, more to the point, only *does* -- &quot;y&quot; facets of a given Sphere, as described...?&quot;. This is exampled in the oft-brought up SoE mage who wants his teleportation platform (Correspondence:4 in Ascension), but doesn't use any of the other facets, at all, of Correspondence:1-3, and can cite in innumerable fictions how the facets described therein -- while metaphysically sound -- aren't employed in said cited fictions, yet &quot;Correspondence:4&quot; still occurs. And that, of course, is just the most *simple* of examples, as there are many, many more, but it drives home the point that while the Spheres give the ideas, the Pillars (or Lesser/Minor Spheres, per STG, or any of a number of terms one might use) actually do a much better job of <i>expressing</i> those ideas within the context of Paradigm, Affinity and applied belief.<br /> <br /> That is, a great many expressions of magical thought/praxis for a number of characters *don't* match up with the scaling/division of the Spheres, at all. <i>At all.</i> Some of the mystical spells/advanced scientific processes/mutant powers/psychic abilities/what-have-you for some characters *aren't* performed at the comparative level indicated by the Spheres: some are more difficult in a given context (requiring a higher level than listed), while others are comparatively simpler (working for the character as a level lower than the one cited, in some cases); some workings are not as complex for some (they don't require having a dozen dots spread among 4-6 Spheres to simulate an given effect, but only a few spread among one or two Pillars, or even just within a single Pillar, if the aspect is appropriately focused within the character's paradigm), while some workings are actually *more* complex (wherein a given effect might be worked per a single Sphere, as presented, but for the mage it requires 3-4 Pillars to simulate). *THAT* is why the Foundation/Pillar system is superior in that regard and actually does a better job of expressing the narratives of Mage than the Sphere system does, as presented: it leaves open a true expression of paradigm for any player who wants to make his mage's magic truly reflective of what he -- player or character -- thinks it should be. The scaling system is still balanced, as the ST would of course still be the final arbiter of what is or isn't allowable, and while the mage may be quite good at things that are strongly in-paradigm for him (aspects that would require an Ascension mage a number of dots in several Spheres to simulate only require the DA:M character a single Pillar), the balance of it all even on a rules level will come to the front as things that are more remote for him (not generally well expressed by his Pillars) either require more dots among Pillars than he may have (just as with Ascension vis-a-vis Spheres) and/or will have a Dif# into the teens, requiring him to use foci, sanctums, conjunctions, Quintessence, Willpower, et al, to a degree that truly makes the effort quite daunting, both by &quot;fluff&quot; and by &quot;numerics&quot; -- more so, readily, than again reflected by Ascension.<br /> <br /> Does it involve a little more work on everybody's parts? Sure. Of course it does. But it also leaves the door much more open for broad creativity and a more truly unique sense of style/flavor for the mages/characters in question. For cross-comparison purposes, any ST worth his salt should be able to recognize the Spheres/Arcana used to create &quot;x&quot; in a given Pillar, either overall or at a specific level, and said ST would also recognize when/where to balance out things if something seems inappropriately &quot;heavy&quot; or &quot;light&quot;, with little more than a few moments glance over the Pillar work-ups. (Sidenote: same thing with the Foundations. If they're treated, say, as &quot;Ranks&quot; are for Garou -- in the sense of &quot;Fostern&quot;, &quot;Adren&quot;, etc., for getting the &quot;gist&quot; of it over for Werewolf players, for example -- then the scaling for that, as well, becomes quite clear, and the *fluff* involved to getting a rating of 4-5 will balance out relative to any XP spent to get there; much like with Humanity/Paths in the 8-10 range, or a Rank of Elder in WW, et al., it isn't something that is achieved, alone, by XP, but a considerable amount of role-playing, as well. That aspect, much like with getting an Arete rating of 6+ -- let alone 9-10, is something that is oft overlooked by many players and a perhaps disturbing number of STs, too....).<br /> <br /> &gt;shrugs&lt; But to each their own. For me and my friends, the Foundation/Pillar system is what Mage should have been about from the start. That is, the descriptors of the Spheres, as presented, would -- as they do -- make a fine example of gauging the relative &quot;weight&quot; of many metaphysical values, but in the end should be used as tools for making/expressing the mage's/character's magic, not the metaphysical paradigm that they are, as written. As stated further up, this does of course make things a little more complicated, but as expressed in Ascension concerning the Spheres -- &quot;...once you get it, it's simpler than it sounds...&quot; the seeming complexity of the Pillars are, in fact, much simpler than they appear, in terms of building/expressing.<br /> <br /> (DISCLAIMER: and, as always, when I use the terms &quot;simple&quot;, and similar, it's always relative to playing a Mage game, regardless of the specific system being used: the game/setting has never, ever been for the &quot;faint of heart&quot;, as it were, in terms of comprehending metaphysical concepts and &quot;thinking outside the box&quot;. All of this is appropriately &quot;geek-level&quot; in terms of discourse, and has been since Day One. But even in that context, a little mental exercise goes a long way to having it all work out... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":1433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","user":"Just John, Forever...","date":".  spacing 03-11-2015, 05:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T15:45:58-07:00","id":437657,"title":"","content":"The Storytellers Handbook gives a good system for replicating Pillars with Spheres (the Minor Spheres), which would work well to reflect the many &quot;Fellowships&quot; within a Tradition. Any such system needs to retain the conceptual flexibility of the Sphere system, of course (as compared to the less-flexible predetermined aspects of Pillars) in order to properly reflect the Ascension setting. But it's a good place to start, especially for STs who don't have the DA books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T17:24:49-07:00","id":437742,"title":"","content":"if im not mistaken the minor pillar system is not like the pillars. that is, a minor sphere is weaker than a sphere, while a pillar is stronger. e.g primus is prime+ a good part of spirit and can be combined with other pillars to do the rest as well as other things.<br /> <br /> in my opinion this is what was missing from dark ages mage:<br /> a <u><b>HUGE</b></u> sidebar explaining how the system works differently from ascension.<br /> <br /> in the core rulebook we had some pretty bad examples. such as&quot;vires 3 and primis 3 can launch a fireball and attack his quintessence at once&quot; well,duh anyone could have seen this.<br /> <br /> or&quot;vires 4 can do a small teleport&quot; that was good in explaining that vires is not just forces but it did not give an explanation on <b>how</b> it is achieved. the vires pillars description simply fails to explain it.<br /> <br /> the pillars descriptions were somewhat vague and unclear. i can see now how primus 2 and corona 3 might do a scrying on location effect but it's not because of the core rulebook.<br /> likewise you could have waterboarded me and i still would not have been able to answer you how a batini heals until the grimoire came out.<br /> <br /> <br /> the difference seems to be that unlike ascension dark ages mage pillars complex spells results seem to be based almost entirely on the metaphysical fluff. e.g the batini convincing his body that his amputaded arm is still there. or perhaps convincing lead that it really is gold a man's bodythat it's female etc.<br /> nothing bad with that approach at all,except it would have helped if the writers had explained it better. it didn't help that most people who bought the books already had our minds &quot;coded&quot; into the ascension system .<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T17:30:29-07:00","id":437756,"title":"","content":"Minor Spheres are like Pillars not where power is concerned, but where scope is concerned: like Pillars, they can combine aspects from more than one Sphere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T21:52:34-07:00","id":438020,"title":"","content":"were there ever any rules on them other than that half page they got on the storyteller handbook?<br /> e.g i don't i saw xp costs for them.<br /> <br /> <i>Chakravanti? Sure, but remember that they're one of many groups during the DA period. The Euthanatos Tradition has not been created yet. In Europe in the period covered by the line, there are:</i><br /> <i># The Knights of St. Gregory of Nyssa (a recognized knightly order that serves as a cover for the worshippers off Radamanthys)</i><br /> <i># The Ixoi (they have not yet split into the Golden Chalice and Ksrafai)</i><br /> <i># The Pomegranate Deme and the The Aided (probably both Old Faith right now, but with a slightly different Foundation. The Aided are actually outcast from the main Old Faith, because they violate the pagan virtues. The Pomegranate Deme are protected by the Gregorian Knights).</i><br /> <i># The Valdaermen (part of the Fellowship is incorporated into the Euthanatos Tradition as the Gallowsmen)</i><br /> <i># The Pollottino family (a small family of &quot;white necromancers who use Etruscan rituals,&quot; and enemies of the Giovanni family)</i><br /> <i>The Chakravanti comprise the:</i><br /> <i># Lahksmists (followers of the divine principle of fortune)</i><br /> <i># Sapindya Sadananda (the Fellowship's warriors and assassins -- also known as the Consanguinity of Eternal Joy. Currently ruled by the necromancer Helekar).</i><br /> <i># Natatapas (your &quot;average&quot; Tantrist Chakravanti, somewhat matrirachal in outlook).</i><br /> <i>We can give them all the same Foundation and Pillars, though.</i><br /> <i>Foundation: Duty (Dharma)</i><br /> <i>The Chakravanti believe that mystical power and enlightenment come through adherence to one's karmically ordained duty. Average people perform the duties mandated by their caste; Chakravanti have the onerous duty of correcting people and groups when they fall astray of that duty through corruption or by clinging to a distraction. When performed correctly, the Chakravat Duty is equated to the positions of the gods and beyond that, the uncreated power that exists beyond the gods. Thus, proper performance of Duty gives godlike attributes.</i><br /> <i>Pillars: Lokha</i><br /> <i>Lokha (worlds) are layers of existence that are both states of being and actual places that the soul (Atman) incarnates. There are six Lokha in total:</i><br /> <i># The demonic Lohka (Naraka)</i><br /> <i># The ghostly Lokha (Preta)</i><br /> <i># The animal Lokha (Triyagoni)</i><br /> <i># The human Lokha (Manu)</i><br /> <i># The Lokha of the warring demigods (Asura)</i><br /> <i># The divine Lokha (Deva)</i><br /> <i>The human Lokha is already within the mage. It is practiced through adherence to Dharma. The Asura Lokha is a false path practiced by other supernatural beings. So the Pillars are:</i><br /> <i># Naraka: Punishment and destruction, cursing.</i><br /> <i># Preta: Necromancy</i><br /> <i># Triyagoni: Healing the body and controlling base desires.</i><br /> <i># Deva: Manipulating the fundamental forces of the universe (like Quintessence), taking in divine characteristics, blessings.</i><br /> <br /> for anyone interested in pillars for the modern euthanatos you could start with this and make what is missing<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","user":"mark","date":". 03-12-2015, 01:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T23:23:26-07:00","id":438090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/435410-da-pillars-for-the-modern-day-traditions?p=438020#post438020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">were there ever any rules on them other than that half page they got on the storyteller handbook?<br /> e.g i don't i saw xp costs for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you need to re-read the section in question.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T01:08:56-07:00","id":438172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is exampled in the oft-brought up SoE mage who wants his teleportation platform (Correspondence:4 in Ascension), but doesn't use any of the other facets, at all, of Correspondence:1-3 </div> </div> </div>But they actually do use those levels, 1-3, in the platform as to teleport something somewhere, especially within SoE's Scientific Paradigm, it needs to sense general spatial relations, to differentiate on target from another to avoid the Fly, and thats Corr 1. t also needs to sense the distances between this place and where it sends it's targets, Corr 2, also before ripping full blown blown gateways that can take multiple passengers one needs to first learn to move simpler objects, Corr 3, and finally once the builder has an understanding over all of that previous data can he use a combination of it to impart it all on his machine that uses Corr 4 to transport multiple objects at once or to create stable portals between places. There is literally no justification in the SoE Paradigm that they could just ignore those requirements and I'm cannot really imagine a Paradigm that would allow transportation without first understanding that which one wishes to transport and of the actual transportation itself.<br /> <br /> It's pretty logical. Even if your paradigm allows teleportation through some less scientific reasons you still need to understand basics instead of jumping straight into the end result. Teleportation in all cases pretty much requires one to have internalized all that comes before it to attempt.<br /> <br /> But like I've said earlier in other threads it's unlikely that we can convince each other of our views and I still posit that the end result is looking and feelings quite similar at our tables despite the underlying system being somewhat different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T01:31:15-07:00","id":438175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thebian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/435410-da-pillars-for-the-modern-day-traditions?p=438090#post438090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you need to re-read the section in question.</div> </div> </div> </div>you are right actually. it costs the same xp. strange.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">&quot;SEERS OF CHRONUS</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">The experience of heightened consciousness is the mead that the Seers </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">of Chronus drink. With laughter and sighs of ecstasy,</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">these wizards of pleasure remake the world not only to accord with </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">their own whims, but to open the eyes of the</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">unenlightened as well. It is with the altered mind that the adept </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">may pierce the veil of ordinary reality and find the paradise</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">concealed within.</span></span><br /> 