e reduced (though</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">ecstatics rarely take this course). New passionate desires may be </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">planted, and though these are usually fleeting, they can be</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">potent enough to cause moving life experiences to others. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">*** Passions roam free amongst the Chronian now. She may appear </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">breathtakingly attractive (temporarily increasing any</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">one of her Social Traits by one dot per success). Radically new </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">desires may be manifested that stand up to time (with a</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">failed Willpower roll) and caution is often thrown to the wind in </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">such cases. In addition, those who enjoy bodily delights</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">with the Seer of Chronus are healed (two bashing or one lethal levels </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">per success). She is often sought after and rarely is a</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">hand raised against her in anger. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">**** Truly magical events occur for those who lie with the Seer now. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">The rapture of lovemaking grants entry into the</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Penumbra for one participant, though only the Seer may lead the way </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">back. Others may become emboldened from the</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">experience (gaining Willpower for each success temporarily). The </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">wizard may even herself serve as a source of Tass in such</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">situations when in intercourse with another willworker (serving as </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">one quintessence for every two successes for the duration</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">of the encounter). </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">***** At last, the Seer of Chronus may awaken the true Aphrodite or </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Adonis within those in the throes of lovemaking.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Unlike before, where only one participant (the Seer or the other(s) </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">engaged with her) would benefit from the casting, now</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">both (or all) involved do so. As the leader of sexual orgies, the </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Seer of Chronus may transport her revelers to other worlds,</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">grant them Willpower, or grant them Tass. She is now the all-high </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Sacred Prostitute, facilitator of pleasure and womb of the</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Gods.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Specialties: Changing Desires, Healing, Empowerment, Seduction</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Sample Foci: Sexual Congress, Seductive Garb</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">SONG</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Insights through music and verse</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">It is said that music can soothe even the most savage soul and yet it </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">can cause tempers to flare and battle to be joined, as</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">well. The whole range of emotions can be served by a clever ditty, a </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">stirring march, or a somber ode. These expressions</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">speak to the very fiber of being and allows enlightenment to arise in </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">an ecstatic way. The Seers of Chronus harness the</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">message in the manner of the mysterious Pan: causing powerful motions </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">to emerge and wisdom to follow.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* The instruction in the ways of Song begins with understanding the </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">emotions that song can give rise to. The Seer may know</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">if a person is simply happy or sad, aggressive or at peace in a way </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">that no subterfuge may hide. This knowledge allows the</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">ecstatic to select the best melody to work with her audience.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">** Now the wizard may augment extant emotions with her song, whether </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">it be through poetry, a tune, or both. She may</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">incite the aggressive to attack with a stirring diatribe or with a </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">insulting song of mockery. She may help the tired to sleep</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">with a lullaby or cause cowards to flee with a mighty crescendo. Song </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">is well known for causing the heart to leap for vaster</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">experience, and the Seers are as well..</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">*** Her expertise in the ways of song now allows her to reverse the </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">song in another\u2019s heart, causing the angry to be calmed</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">or the pacifistic to be readied for action (both of which can be </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">resisted with Willpower). Hypnotic melodies can dull an</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">audience\u2019s mind, making them unlikely to be wary, and battle marches </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">can help warriors to victory (adding one temporary</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">dot of Dexterity per success). Her understanding of the music in </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">other\u2019s hearts grows, as well (adding two temporary dots of</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Empathy per success). Those suffering under an unpleasant song (a </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">continuing mental enchantment) may be freed from such</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">constraints (dispersing such magics on a one-for-one basis).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">**** Truly mind-bending compositions are now within the Seer\u2019s </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">purview. Those unwilling to partake of merriment may be</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">forced into a wild dance or a painful song (being able to do nothing </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">else and taking one level bashing damage for as long as</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">the enchantment lasts). Or be maddened by her sorcerous sonatas </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">(temporarily losing 2 dots of Intelligence per success).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Energies flow from the wizard\u2019s vocalizations, drawing forth the </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">ecstasy within the crowd.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">***** The right song can change a life, for better for ill. Her </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">haunting melodies lure crowds of people into certain mindsets,</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">which tend to last (affecting two people per success). Tantamount to </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">the Muses, the Seer may work her Song in with another</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">ensorcelment and grant it greater life (doubling the duration of a </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">complex spell) or permanently enlightening another</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">(granting them 1 dot in one Ability, may only be used on the same </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">person thrice).. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Specialties: Encouraging emotions, Forcing performance, Lengthening </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">spells, Dispelling mind effects</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Sample Foci: Musical instruments, Singing</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">TIME</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Insights through time distortion</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">The Pillar of Grandfather Chronus himself, Time serves to enlighten </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">all in ecstatic certainty. What occurs in one\u2019s life</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">manifests very profound lessons that none may ignore. And by seeing </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">time as it really is; that is fluid, the willworker can</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">gasp and feel the potency of the ages upon her. For all things that </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">are, once were, and all things that once were, are yet to</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">come to pass.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">* The Seer begins by understanding the essential passage of time. She </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">may sense when major events are ordained to happen</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">(though she has little idea of the specifics) and when time itself </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">has been altered. Though she knows that time is essentially</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">subjective, she can translate that perception into its objective </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">corollary (and keep a highly accurate time).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">** Now the ecstatic can prevent others from affecting time (causing </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">successes that ward against temporal magic) and gain a</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">clearer understanding of what the future holds (with successes </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">equating to a longer and more accurate vision). The timelines</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">of individuals start to become apparent to her also, and she can gain </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">glimpses into someone\u2019s past, present, or future.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">*** With ecstatic insight, the wizard may now affect the clock of </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Grandfather Time in small, general ways. She may slow its</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">advance (allowing her to take an extra action for every two successes </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">scored) or speed its pace (causing a small area to</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">appear frozen for a turn or two, while the rest of creation advances </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">as normal). Though impressive at this level of mastery,</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">the Seer is forbidden to otherwise affect or allow those frozen to be </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">affected, or else earn the enmity of mighty Chronus</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">himself.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">**** Specific streams of time become easier for the Seer to affect </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">now. She may cause the speed of individual objects, such</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">as arrows or claws, to be slowed (making two objects harmless per </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">success) or to increase their velocity by shortening its</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">time line (and causing one to object to double the strength of its </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">impact per success). Certain beings may be frozen in place</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">(resisted with Willpower) while she and others are free to act upon </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">those beings with impunity (the 3 dot restriction is now</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">lifted). She may read the past and present circumstances of </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">individuals fully now, much as the Fates may do, and see some</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">of the possible futures that are in store for them (with increasing </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">clarity per success).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">***** The near-complete mastery of Time is within the Seer\u2019s grasp </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">now. As a true daughter of Chronus, she can step away</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">from the normal passage of time, while others remain adrift in it. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">The world may become as one of statues for her (granting</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">her one turn per success scored to act while others are frozen ) or </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">she may choose a more fitting time for her to dwell instead</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">(traveling forward or backward in time to an increasing extent per </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">success).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Specialties: Fortune telling, Affecting the motion of objects, </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Freezing foes, Traveling through time.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Sample Foci: Hallucinogens, Deep meditation, Strict hedonistic </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">regimens. &quot;<br /> <br /> i am not sure who wrote this but it sure looks nice. hope it helps</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T16:38:19-07:00","id":439043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/435410-da-pillars-for-the-modern-day-traditions?p=438020#post438020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">were there ever any rules on them other than that half page they got on the storyteller handbook?<br /> e.g i don't i saw xp costs for them.<br /> <br /> <i>Chakravanti? Sure, but remember that they're one of many groups during the DA period. The Euthanatos Tradition has not been created yet. In Europe in the period covered by the line, there are:</i><br /> <i># The Knights of St. Gregory of Nyssa (a recognized knightly order that serves as a cover for the worshippers off Radamanthys)</i><br /> <i># The Ixoi (they have not yet split into the Golden Chalice and Ksrafai)</i><br /> <i># The Pomegranate Deme and the The Aided (probably both Old Faith right now, but with a slightly different Foundation. The Aided are actually outcast from the main Old Faith, because they violate the pagan virtues. The Pomegranate Deme are protected by the Gregorian Knights).</i><br /> <i># The Valdaermen (part of the Fellowship is incorporated into the Euthanatos Tradition as the Gallowsmen)</i><br /> <i># The Pollottino family (a small family of &quot;white necromancers who use Etruscan rituals,&quot; and enemies of the Giovanni family)</i><br /> <i>The Chakravanti comprise the:</i><br /> <i># Lahksmists (followers of the divine principle of fortune)</i><br /> <i># Sapindya Sadananda (the Fellowship's warriors and assassins -- also known as the Consanguinity of Eternal Joy. Currently ruled by the necromancer Helekar).</i><br /> <i># Natatapas (your &quot;average&quot; Tantrist Chakravanti, somewhat matrirachal in outlook).</i><br /> <i>We can give them all the same Foundation and Pillars, though.</i><br /> <i>Foundation: Duty (Dharma)</i><br /> <i>The Chakravanti believe that mystical power and enlightenment come through adherence to one's karmically ordained duty. Average people perform the duties mandated by their caste; Chakravanti have the onerous duty of correcting people and groups when they fall astray of that duty through corruption or by clinging to a distraction. When performed correctly, the Chakravat Duty is equated to the positions of the gods and beyond that, the uncreated power that exists beyond the gods. Thus, proper performance of Duty gives godlike attributes.</i><br /> <i>Pillars: Lokha</i><br /> <i>Lokha (worlds) are layers of existence that are both states of being and actual places that the soul (Atman) incarnates. There are six Lokha in total:</i><br /> <i># The demonic Lohka (Naraka)</i><br /> <i># The ghostly Lokha (Preta)</i><br /> <i># The animal Lokha (Triyagoni)</i><br /> <i># The human Lokha (Manu)</i><br /> <i># The Lokha of the warring demigods (Asura)</i><br /> <i># The divine Lokha (Deva)</i><br /> <i>The human Lokha is already within the mage. It is practiced through adherence to Dharma. The Asura Lokha is a false path practiced by other supernatural beings. So the Pillars are:</i><br /> <i># Naraka: Punishment and destruction, cursing.</i><br /> <i># Preta: Necromancy</i><br /> <i># Triyagoni: Healing the body and controlling base desires.</i><br /> <i># Deva: Manipulating the fundamental forces of the universe (like Quintessence), taking in divine characteristics, blessings.</i><br /> <br /> for anyone interested in pillars for the modern euthanatos you could start with this and make what is missing<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And, by direct implication, completely ignore the paradigms of all the other groups you list? Unless you are saying that, at the foundation of the Euthanatos Tradition, the Chakravanti essentially inculcated their paradigm into all the other groups that were thrown together? What about the groups added into the Euthanatos that were from outside Eurasia (or precisely from the list above most of Europe &amp; the Indian sub-continent)? What about Near &amp; Middle Eastern, North &amp; South American or African groups that joined &quot;Team Euthanatos&quot;? <br /> <br /> It's almost as bad as the muddled mess of the Old Faith and the Spirit-talkers, which are pretty much exactly &quot;proto-Verbena&quot; and &quot;proto-Spirit-talkers&quot; (but just for Europeans for both). Both the Old Faith and the Spirit-talkers are huge amalgams of many very different paradigms that have been painted over so heavily with a broad brush they are effectively spackled together. Some of the &quot;regional variants&quot; in both Fellowships are more different from each other than either are from the Order of Hermes or than the Order of Hermes is from the Ahl-i-Batin. In essence, both of them are actually Traditions instead of Fellowships. With all of a modern Tradition's lack of subtlety in it's paradigm, over-generalization and non-paradigm-specific rules build that the OP wanted to replace. <br /> <br /> There's a reason for the Sphere system once you try to go to an interactive global setting. You could do Fellowship/Foundation/Pillar but, to be really fair, you need to do 100's of them. Then Traditions would be groups of like-minded Fellowships with Foundations and/or Pillars of similar resonance being grouped together. (With a heavy scoop of political in-fighting). Crafts would be Fellowships that didn't join up. Orphans would be.... hmmm.... not sure. <br /> <br /> Or you can just get out the old broad paint brush and the spackle and erase any inconvenient differences. In which case, it seems, to me, you've lost the whole point of what the Fellowship/Foundation/Pillar brings to the table, the integration of paradigm in the RAW a manifest and meaningful way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T14:37:03-07:00","id":440482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/435410-da-pillars-for-the-modern-day-traditions?p=438172#post438172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...It's pretty logical. Even if your paradigm allows teleportation through some less scientific reasons you still need to understand basics instead of jumping straight into the end result. Teleportation in all cases pretty much requires one to have internalized all that comes before it to attempt..</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily (and, in some cases, <i>not at all</i>). It is entirely possible for a given mage to have, say, the teleportation effect of Correspondence:4 *without* possessing the other aspects of the previous levels (individualized teleportation, mulit-vector spatial awareness -- hell, spatial awareness <i>of any kind</i>, for that matter -- the ability to scry locations, or any of several others) -- it just makes the Effect <i>more dangerous. </i>It also side-steps the point I'm trying to make, which I'll illustrate via other examples as -- I suspect -- my &quot;oft-cited SoE&quot; example (which was an ongoing topic for a number of people back in the 90's, on this forums-then incarnation, as well as several WoD-related conventions) is not illustrating the point very well, due perhaps to its (my) dated reference...<br /> <br /> A specific example brought up at several conventions was how to simulate Star Trek-style transporters, as they most emphatically don't operate on the Correspondence:4 principles. I provided the definitive answer at two of the conventions: Life:4 (transforming/altering simple-to-complex living patterns), Matter:4 (ditto for non-living materials), Forces:5 (the energy transformation of said targets, as well as the force-fields involved that have demonstrated as being able to mitigate extreme outside energy interference on a number -- not all, but a number -- of occasions, including matter-anti-matter explosions) and Correspondence:2 (targeting a given location via sensors and micro-&quot;pricking&quot; of subspace to allow matter-energy stream transmission). That isn't Correspondence:4, not by a mile, even with the sliver-cut piece provided by Correspondence:2. I cite that because *that* fit the conceptual idea to a T, as well as fitting the broader paradigm of not only a great number of Technocratic paradigms, but a number of SoE characters, as well.<br /> <br /> It's not a question of whether or not the Spheres, as presented, make metaphysical sense -- they do, absolutely. No question. The issue more comes about that as presented, <i>they are just another paradigm-expression for how the concepts listed can be expressed or delineated.</i> Correspondence, at lower levels, provides scrying of localities (C-2). Not all mages will have that in their paradigm (Messianic Voices, for example, in any direct form), but they may have teleportation (Gavri-El:4, and applying to the character, himself) anyway, via a different metaphysical means. Depending on the fluff, this may make the teleportation more dangerous, and/or require certain circumstances (use of sad ability in the service of God, as opposed to more base uses), or conversely simply &quot;work&quot; via spiritual guidance, therefore safe-guarding against mishap (and, again, not requiring previous levels/abilities indicated by Correspondence). On a related note, it can also be that the ability to teleport, say, others (something doable with C-4) also isn't included, as presented, in someone's paradigm (as is the case, again, with the Voices), but rather requires additional support from another pillar, based on a metaphysical concept which, again, is *not* related to C-4 (in this case, the Messianic would apply Gavri-El:4s teleportation to another via Mika-El:2, for a willing/unconscious target, or Mika-El:4 to compel the target's presence -- to or away; in that regard, it's the underlying ability to apply conceptual command to a situation that allows Gavri-El:4 to teleport another, *not* any additional principle as laid out in Correspondence:4...). The result may be the same, but the means-and-methods are quite different, both by fluff and by game mechanics (the crunch).<br /> <br /> <i>That's the point</i>. <br /> <br /> Ascensions Spheres operate on the underlying principle that *every* aspect of *every* Sphere is discernible and achievable in each Traditions paradigm(s), and that they are ultimately achieved (by relation) by way of the same &quot;degree&quot; and effectiveness (relative to how the Spheres are presented/delineated).<br /> <br /> Bullshit.<br /> <br /> Complete and utter bullshit.<br /> <br /> *That* conceptual error is why so many questions came up so often in the 90s (and since) relative to &quot;but my mage's magic doesn't work that way... and it doesn't work that way in [fill in blank of movie/book/tv show/what-have-you] that I am trying to simulate... yet this whole &quot;Paradigm&quot; thing keeps getting pushed hard... but I can't seem to do &quot;xyz&quot; with the Spheres, as presented...&quot;, which I can personally vouch for as having shown up on the forums at the top and bottom of the hour. But you *can* simulate [ ] much more closely by making a set of Pillars to reflect more accurately the metaphysical paradigm in the character's/player's mind(s). *Much* more closely.<br /> <br /> Some aspects, for some mages, simply aren't as easy as the Spheres indicate (a proto-SoE from the *proper* Steampunk Era -- which wouldn't be the late Victorian, as some misperceive, but from the late 1600's thru the 1700's, during Enlightenment -- would, per my write-up for a friend, use Dynamics, Odyllics and Synergies to simulate teleportation, as such would truly be more difficult that via just a single Sphere/Pillar, alone, for them). On the flip (and more on-point for many mages), there are a number of Effects that are *easier* to work than indicated via the Spheres : my character, Andreas, has a natural penchant for perceptual/divinatory magics, and his Clairsentience Pillar has a range from &quot;just a touch&quot; to &quot;a nice slice&quot; of aspects that would require a number of Spheres to simulate... but he doesn't have any of the other aspects associated with those Spheres, which would be &quot;out-of-paradigm&quot; for him, contextually speaking, so for example if he wanted to work a divination that let him know mystical powers were at work (Prime:1) at several of his/his friends homes (Correspondence:3), whether or not those forces game from this or the other side of the Gauntlet (Spirit:1-2, depending on areas), and whether those forces were going to have a detrimental influence on him/them (Time:2 w/ Entropy:1, the latter helping make clearer his visions of the future) and what their intentions were (Mind:3), that would require 12 dots in Spheres (and, within the context of Ascension's designed paradigm, that would be correct. *However*, for Andreas, he can accomplish that with Clairsentience:3. (Of course, said Pillar doesn't let him &quot;do&quot; anything, actively, except in rarer instances... but then, that's the point of the Pillar: it's utility, in Andreas' paradigm, is the considerable awareness and understanding it provides/he achieves through it, not whether it lets him &quot;do&quot; anything, actively, as such...).<br /> <br /> *THAT* is how the concepts in Ascensions Spheres are *properly* manifested through the various paradigms: the overall concepts/Effects are recognizable, but their implementation (including the &quot;color of methodology&quot; actually resulting in a &quot;different game mechanic&quot;, in a number of Paradigms) is often very, very different. The Pillars go a long, long way towards having both fluff *and* game mechanics reflect this.<br /> <br /> Just saying...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T15:52:27-07:00","id":440539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just saying... </div> </div> </div>We get that you don't agree from the massive post. You don't need to be passive aggressive about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T15:55:18-07:00","id":440543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/435410-da-pillars-for-the-modern-day-traditions?p=440482#post440482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ascensions Spheres operate on the underlying principle that *every* aspect of *every* Sphere is discernible and achievable in each Traditions paradigm(s), and that they are ultimately achieved (by relation) by way of the same &quot;degree&quot; and effectiveness (relative to how the Spheres are presented/delineated).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure it's as cut and dried as this. Certainly the rules <i>ultimately</i> allow for a mage to cast any Effect, but there is a fair amount of word-count dedicated to the idea that not every Effect is discernible and achievable in each Paradigm. The various sections on Paradigms and Styles talk about how certain Effects may not be possible under a given paradigm or style, for example. And different paradigms or styles do deal with different Effects in different ways, with different degrees of effectiveness - your teleportation example shows that, as does the old Lady Into Tiger thing.<br /> <br /> I do agree that bespoke Pillars are a better way of depicting this kind of thing, but I think you're being a tad dismissive of Ascension's attempts to address the issue <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T16:30:50-07:00","id":440584,"title":"","content":"The long and short of it is that Foundations and Pillars are really great if you can keep down the number of different options open as character choices down. Then you can plumb the depths of a paradigm and intricately and specifically tailor the rules and the paradigm together. <br /> <br /> But, when you try to have Foundations and Pillars replace Spheres, if you look at the constituency in any Tradition or Convention, you're going to need multiple different combinations of multiple different Foundations and multiple different Pillars to accurately portray the membership of these trans-ethnic global sodalities that were brought together by some spectrum of shared interests, a few similarities in outlook and a lot of politics and accidents of history. Moreover, some Foundations and some Pillars are going to cross-over between sub-groups that parallel each other in completely different Traditions and Conventions. <br /> <br /> Or else you just need to pull out the spackle gun, aim at all the different subgroups and twist the setting dial over to &quot;Euthanatos&quot; or &quot;Verbena&quot; or &quot;Iteration X&quot; and then glom together a wide variety of very different groups together under one onerous Foundation/Pillar system. Why onerous? Because you are going to be erasing all the important distinctions (i.e. paradigms) between the sub-groups by doing so and, thereby, loosing the thing that the Fellowship Foundation/Pillar system does SO WELL, integrating paradigms and mechanics. <br /> <br /> There are some things that the Foundation/Pillar system does VERY WELL, but there are some things the Sphere system does better. Not being able to access every possible power mentioned in each and every dot of a Sphere because you can't manage a way to wrap your paradigm about it isn't a weakness of the Sphere system. It's a part of dealing with the limitations inherent in a character and every character is going to have limitations. It's just not a thing written into the Sphere rules as explicitly as it is in the Foundation/Pillar rules. With Spheres, that sort of limitation has to be negotiated on a case-by-case basis by the gaming group in question. Which also happens with the Foundation/Pillar system. (As we have CERTAINLY seen threads about &quot;How do I do this?&quot; in DA Mage magic). And, in a larger sense, is the thing that really sets all flavors of Mage apart from other most games.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T16:42:43-07:00","id":440622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/435410-da-pillars-for-the-modern-day-traditions?p=440584#post440584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not being able to access every possible power mentioned in each and every dot of a Sphere because you can't manage a way to wrap your paradigm about it isn't a weakness of the Sphere system. It's a part of dealing with the limitations inherent in a character and every character is going to have limitations. It's just not a thing written into the Sphere rules as explicitly as it is in the Foundation/Pillar rules. With Spheres, that sort of limitation has to be negotiated on a case-by-case basis by the gaming group in question. Which also happens with the Foundation/Pillar system. (As we have CERTAINLY seen threads about &quot;How do I do this?&quot; in DA Mage magic). And, in a larger sense, is the thing that really sets all flavors of Mage apart from other most games.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. In fact, the back-and-forth negotiation and exploration of what each paradigm can do is part of what makes Mage fun for me. It's something that helps each group make the game their own. I love it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T19:10:09-07:00","id":440778,"title":"","content":"according to dark ages mage core rule book :dark ages magick is dynamic within a static framework.<br /> <br /> i think the overall idea is that from a metagame perspective back at that time the fellowships were just<b> wrong</b> about certain things.<br /> this is however the time were cross fellowship cabals are becoming more popular.<br /> so presumably by 1466(though it could have taken more time) the mages had workes out these mistakes.<br /> if youre a batini and watch,for 200 years the average hermetic effortlessly heal himself eventually you'll think: maybe im doing it wrong.<br /> likewise said messianic voice/choristers could learn a lot from the batini for the non teleportative aspects of (what is effectively) correspondence.<br /> <br /> at any rate though even in modern mage it's explicitly mentioned that you can't do every single thing that could be possible by your spheres just by having them.<br /> for instance celestial chorus revised has a paradox mitigating rote explicitly stating that it would be very hard for others to do it.<br /> <br /> likewise while a technocrat can increase his physical attributes it takes(according to a recent book) a lot of time per dot.<br /> and while they technically have the spirit(even if called otherwise) sphere almost all of them would be unable to brand an avatar. because it doesn't exist to them.<br /> or&quot; a verbena would propably be unable to transform a fera into a claypot. <br /> paradigm restrictions still do apply it's just that after 500 years of contact they are not as many as they used to be.<br /> and they can be worked out by player effort.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T01:48:51-07:00","id":441082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/435410-da-pillars-for-the-modern-day-traditions?p=440778#post440778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">according to dark ages mage core rule book :dark ages magick is dynamic within a static framework.<br /> <br /> i think the overall idea is that from a metagame perspective back at that time the fellowships were just<b> wrong</b> about certain things.<br /> this is however the time were cross fellowship cabals are becoming more popular.<br /> so presumably by 1466(though it could have taken more time) the mages had workes out these mistakes.<br /> if youre a batini and watch,for 200 years the average hermetic effortlessly heal himself eventually you'll think: maybe im doing it wrong.<br /> likewise said messianic voice/choristers could learn a lot from the batini for the non teleportative aspects of (what is effectively) correspondence.<br /> <br /> at any rate though even in modern mage it's explicitly mentioned that you can't do every single thing that could be possible by your spheres just by having them.<br /> for instance celestial chorus revised has a paradox mitigating rote explicitly stating that it would be very hard for others to do it.<br /> <br /> likewise while a technocrat can increase his physical attributes it takes(according to a recent book) a lot of time per dot.<br /> and while they technically have the spirit(even if called otherwise) sphere almost all of them would be unable to brand an avatar. because it doesn't exist to them.<br /> or&quot; a verbena would propably be unable to transform a fera into a claypot.<br /> paradigm restrictions still do apply it's just that after 500 years of contact they are not as many as they used to be.<br /> and they can be worked out by player effort.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is exacly what im trying to say, though the Spheres kinda lend themselves to &quot;I can do eit because the book says i can do it if i have this Sphere at this level&quot; Instead of the Pillars &quot;I can't do that because its not explicitly stated in the books&quot;.<br /> <br /> Perhaps what i'm looking for is a system where you take the Spheres as a framework but write for each Tradition a set of &quot;This is something the Tradition is very good at&quot; and &quot;This is something this Tradition hasn't figured out how to do yet&quot;. Or rewrite the Spheres to be special for each Tradition. Sorta like Dim Sci, Data, Machine etc.<br /> <br /> For example: what Spheres does the Order of Hermes have access to in its totality? Which Spheres do they only have access to certain aspects of etc.? Can the Order do everything described in the Sphere writeup for Forces? No? What can they do and what can't they do? How about Spirit? Entropy? Time?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T03:09:49-07:00","id":441141,"title":"","content":"the hermetics are propably(always talking about the average person) less good at entropy and time than say,the euthanatos. for instance they would propably be more focused on the fate(like in awakening) aspect of entropy that decay. likewise most of them tend to interact with the spirit umbrood more.though these are propably less of a case of restriction and more of personal choic in their part.<br /> <br /> your average hermetic propably can't make a laser beam as we modern people understand it. likewise even a master of matter may have some difficulty creating antimatter with just matter 5. at the very least not without a lot of scientific knowledge and some work. <br /> <br /> it's just that these restrictions are not carved in stone. in the same way that technically speaking only arete is needed to be a mage. but we all know that a hermetic with tertiary mental attributes and intelligence of 1-2 tertiary knowledges and no linguistics enochian and occult at all makes absolutely no sense.<br /> or imagine a progenitor master who couldn't close a wound(medicine) if his life depended on it.<br /> <br /> <br /> in the dark ages the average hermetic might thinnk that doing x is impossible. but in the modern age if he has seen someone do it then he knows that his magic theory needs some work.<br /> <br /> <br /> to give a (i hope) helpful real life example. in the dark ages the catholic church &quot;knew&quot; that the earth was some thousand years old. you would not even consider arguing about it. the same is not true today.<br /> <br /> back to the hermetics they are a curious case because theirs is propably the most flexible paradigm.<br /> <br /> <br /> after all their paradigm is:knowledge,i use the spirits/gods not serve them or they are abstract symbold using the principle of etc. , my will be done and the world be damned, reason combined with mystical knowledge as well as getting the &quot;best of&quot; from every other group(from their cold dead hands if it has to be so) removing blind superstition and hermeticising them. the tremere are a fine example of this approach.<br /> were this a game like mage the awakening where(from what little i know of it) there <b> is</b> a secret real truth hidden some where then the order would indeed be the most correct organisation.<br /> of course ascension is a bit more complicated like that.<br /> <br /> any way concerning your original question if the pillars i posted were any help, i think i can find some more(theyr just buried in my pc somewhere<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T08:48:21-07:00","id":441358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/435410-da-pillars-for-the-modern-day-traditions?p=441082#post441082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;I can do eit because the book says i can do it if i have this Sphere at this level&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Players like this are usually pretty new to Mage and don't understand the articulation between their paradigm and the Sphere system or they want to play a very different game than my players and I usually are going for. Usually, in my experience, they are the later and they are coming from a power-gamer place, causing much gnashing of the teeth and tearing at the hair and beard and ending in a parting of the ways.<br /> <br /> Not to say that it might not be an interesting and very surreal game to minimize paradigms and play a game of a group of dreamy, reality-twisting wish-crafti, but that would be a very specific game and would be taking the Mage rules and doing something off the beaten path with them. Something that might be very cool with the right group of people. Like the dreams of the mutant love-child of the Promethea comic and Love in the time of Cholera.... <br /> <br /> But that's not the point, they usually want to play the equivalent of superheroes with the Cosmic Cube/Power Cosmic/Power Ring/whatever.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T15:14:41-07:00","id":441878,"title":"","content":"My own approach to this issue is to riff off of the Techcratic Sphere variants. Yes, the Traditions have a set of nine Spheres that, in theory, any mage can learn and use; but as I see it, many (most?) of these Spheres are so widely applicable because they\u2019re <i>compromises</i>, designed by committee to more or less fit as many of the Traditions\u2019 various paradigms as possible. However, each Tradition has its own ideas of what a given Sphere <i>ought to be</i> like, which doesn\u2019t always line up with how that Sphere is normally taught. Those Traditions have developed customized variants of those Spheres where they think that the \u201cgeneric\u201d version missed the point. That\u2019s where the Machine Sphere came from: the notion that the Sons of Ether and Iteration X needed something that was less about chemistry and more about mechanics. <br /> <br /> I tend to avoid completely restructuring the organizing principle of the Nine Spheres, at least as far as the Traditions go; every Sphere variant stands in for one of the existing Spheres. And I try to limit each Tradition to two or three Sphere variants, while having them use regular Spheres for everything else. Heck, even their custom Spheres aren\u2019t universally used by their membership; though the extent to which the custom spheres replace the generic ones varies from Tradition to Tradition. My rationale is that the Traditions are a sect that was founded on finding common ground; and the Nine Spheres form that common ground. The Technocracy likewise uses a very similar set of Spheres, but with their own technomantic tweaks to them. <br /> <br /> OTOH, I\u2019m all for different organizing principles when it comes to the Disparates. For instance, I have no problem with the notion that the Sisters of Hypollyta study the Seasons instead of the Spheres; and I\u2019d be perfectly fine with the Templars calling on Archangels instead of wielding Spheres. I suspect that with a little effort, every set of Pillars described in <b>Dark Ages: Mage</b> could find a home with a modern Disparate faction. They are, after all, Disparates; being at odds with the way the Traditions do things is <i>what they do</i>. And Disparates that don\u2019t practice DAMage Pillars may well practice <i>their own</i> Pillars. One wonders what the Wu Lung Pillars might look like\u2026<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve also toyed with the notion of replacing Arete with Foundations, with most Traditions and Crafts getting thier own Foundation. (In keeping with their \u201cOne True Way\u201d mentality, Technocrats all share a common Foundation: Enlightenment.) For this notion, I scrap the \u201cTenth Sphere\u201d talk as a setting element and instead look to what the published material has to say about Tenth Spheres as inspiration for devising the various Traditions\u2019 Foundations \u2014 in a manner of speaking, the Foundation a mage uses <i>is</i> his \u201cTenth Sphere\u201d. <br /> <br /> I discuss much of this in my Ascension Hacks, linked to in my sig.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-14-2015, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T16:18:19-07:00","id":441939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/435410-da-pillars-for-the-modern-day-traditions?p=440539#post440539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We get that you don't agree from the massive post. You don't need to be passive aggressive about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>? There's nothing passive-aggressive about my saying &quot;just saying...&quot;, at all. I've ended a great number of posts on the various incarnations of this forum for 2 decades now in that manner, usually as a &quot;blunter&quot; to counter-point the fact that a post I've made may come across as heated, dismissive or otherwise inflammatory in some regard. As for my post being massive, it's a Catch-22: if I go short, then the various points/counterpoints concerning &quot;xyz&quot; aren't covered, or exampled, and all it does is add fuel to the fire of &quot;yeah-hunh/nuh-uh&quot; that often goes on; if I elaborate with examples and cited points, then the post, by its nature, will be comparatively long... and somebody will comment on that (the length) as opposed to actually addressing the substance of what was posted.<br /> <br /> <i>Just saying</i>...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T16:42:29-07:00","id":449893,"title":"","content":"i've used the minor spheres instead of the major spheres and the pillars in both modern and dark ages games<br /> <br /> i had to write all my own material for them and it was a pain in the ass.<br /> <br /> I'm still running the dark ages chronicle, it's 25 sessions in and I've got to say it's been tough to try and add more minor spheres, I actually could use some help with that so I'll be posting for suggestions soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","name":"Dream_Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T20:06:44-07:00","id":915319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dream_Walker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/435410-da-pillars-for-the-modern-day-traditions?p=449893#post449893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i've used the minor spheres instead of the major spheres and the pillars in both modern and dark ages games<br /> <br /> i had to write all my own material for them and it was a pain in the ass.<br /> <br /> I'm still running the dark ages chronicle, it's 25 sessions in and I've got to say it's been tough to try and add more minor spheres, I actually could use some help with that so I'll be posting for suggestions soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Rise, Necro-Thread -- RISE...)<br /> <br /> (Here because Mark linked via another post, and as I must not have seen your response -- and it coincidentally happens to jibe with some other discussion in other threads -- I'll go ahead and resurrect this for a moment...)<br /> <br /> The thing is, it &quot;shouldn't&quot; be that hard to create/use Minor Spheres in a DA setting (or any Mage setting, for that matter) because the gist of the &quot;minor&quot; Spheres is essentially what is used to create the Pillars, only a step more simple. You take pieces of different Spheres and sew them together under a different over-arcing metaphysical (P)aradigm than as-presented by the Sphere System. Easy. (Pillars are a step more complex because Paradigm(tm) is more intently stressed, and that leads to occasionally a given metaphysical concept being placed a higher-or-lower scale-wise on the 1-5 rating -- or becoming more inclusive or diffuse along a given set of Pillars -- which doesn't normally occur with the Minor Sphere approach, which pieces things together on the same &quot;level&quot; as indicated in the Sphere System).<br /> <br /> Honestly, though, 'porting in Minor Spheres should be the easiest thing for a given character/mage, as they are conceptually much easier to make than Pillars (if consequently comparatively less flexible than the latter).<br /> <br /> If you read this -- as it's been over a year since your post -- let me/us know if things have gotten easier for you, and if not do you still want some help/advice....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T06:39:47-07:00","id":915561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/435410-da-pillars-for-the-modern-day-traditions?p=915319#post915319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Rise, Necro-Thread -- RISE...)<br /> <br /> (Here because Mark linked via another post, and as I must not have seen your response -- and it coincidentally happens to jibe with some other discussion in other threads -- I'll go ahead and resurrect this for a moment...)<br /> <br /> The thing is, it &quot;shouldn't&quot; be that hard to create/use Minor Spheres in a DA setting (or any Mage setting, for that matter) because the gist of the &quot;minor&quot; Spheres is essentially what is used to create the Pillars, only a step more simple. You take pieces of different Spheres and sew them together under a different over-arcing metaphysical (P)aradigm than as-presented by the Sphere System. Easy. (Pillars are a step more complex because Paradigm(tm) is more intently stressed, and that leads to occasionally a given metaphysical concept being placed a higher-or-lower scale-wise on the 1-5 rating -- or becoming more inclusive or diffuse along a given set of Pillars -- which doesn't normally occur with the Minor Sphere approach, which pieces things together on the same &quot;level&quot; as indicated in the Sphere System).<br /> <br /> Honestly, though, 'porting in Minor Spheres should be the easiest thing for a given character/mage, as they are conceptually much easier to make than Pillars (if consequently comparatively less flexible than the latter).<br /> <br /> If you read this -- as it's been over a year since your post -- let me/us know if things have gotten easier for you, and if not do you still want some help/advice....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> i would also add that minor spheres are a bit less &quot;abstract&quot; for instance while you could make a &quot;divination&quot; or ephemera&quot; minor sphere you wouldn't make &quot;spring&quot; or summer&quot;<br /> though i suppose certain pillars(e.g al hajj al anbiya vires primus etc ) might as well be called &quot;greater spheres)<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> the &quot;trick&quot; in the minor sphere system is correctly conceptualising them. for instance in the &quot;fire&quot; minor sphere&quot; i would change the rank 5 power&quot; font of paradise for fire only&quot; to&quot; turning stuff into fire and fire into stuff.<br /> granted this included a small part of the matter sphere and not just life but in my opinion(especially for something so limited as &quot;fire&quot; which shows an extremely obsessed mage if you ask me)<br /> <br /> the rule that you can only take 2 aspects of a sphere per rank is not supposed to be written in stone. it should be seen on a case by case basis.<br /> e.g i find it strange that a minor sphere of fire can't actually conjure fire!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> i would also rule that perhaps instead of putting 2 rank 5 effects in the minor sphere rank of 5 you could,say put 1 rank 5 and 2 rank 3. or something like that.<br /> or you might make certain ranks of a minor sphere weak and others &quot;Explode&quot; not just for balance but also if it fits the concept of the minor sphere you create<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T13:09:55-07:00","id":915791,"title":"","content":"I think one of the really cool things with the Sphere system is that it implies that Technocrats and Traditionalists who switch to the other side will instinctively and easily 'get' certain things. For example, the former NWO Operative who used Correspondence: Data...as a newly christened Verbena, he will surprisingly fast get how to become in tune with sacred grove of his Cabal to appear in the sacred grove of another Verbena Cabal :-). (whether due to a wholesale teleport, or with a co-location)<br /> I actually think this is how it should be. Guess I'm a believer in the Sphere system/Paradigm :-).<br /> (But yes, it is kind of ridiculous. Or maybe simply funny.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 06-16-2016, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T02:08:06-07:00","id":916086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/435410-da-pillars-for-the-modern-day-traditions?p=915791#post915791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think one of the really cool things with the Sphere system is that it implies that Technocrats and Traditionalists who switch to the other side will instinctively and easily 'get' certain things. For example, the former NWO Operative who used Correspondence: Data...as a newly christened Verbena, he will surprisingly fast get how to become in tune with sacred grove of his Cabal to appear in the sacred grove of another Verbena Cabal :-). (whether due to a wholesale teleport, or with a co-location)<br /> I actually think this is how it should be. Guess I'm a believer in the Sphere system/Paradigm :-).<br /> (But yes, it is kind of ridiculous. Or maybe simply funny.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> actually according to the mage st handbook a complete paradigm swap will require your mage to rebuy the spheres at half the listed cost.<br /> <br /> it's e very good way of illustrating that the older and more powerful mages become &quot;set&quot; in their ways. which is why we'll never ever see voormas becoming an akashic.<br /> <br /> think of it like that let's say you can either be a brawler or a martial artist.<br /> you have 1 point in brawl and want to swap;. at that point it;s east<br /> <br /> but ... if you have 5 points in brawl. are you really going to consider it&quot; especially since at that point picking new things is hard for you.<br /> <br /> one of the problems with the sphere system is that it essentially forces you to learn things that don't really fit your character's paradigm at all. in some cases they may be the majority. plus you get people relatively new to the game which assume that just because it;s in the sphere description or theyve seen it in a book somewhere they can do it.<br /> <br /> the other problem is(At least in my opinion) that the game sort of loses flavour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","user":"mark","date":". 06-17-2016, 05:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T02:23:26-07:00","id":916091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/435410-da-pillars-for-the-modern-day-traditions?p=916086#post916086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">actually according to the mage st handbook a complete paradigm swap will require your mage to rebuy the spheres at half the listed cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly my point. &quot;At half the listed cost&quot; - the former NWO (or former Syndic with Correspondence foci of &quot;people management&quot;) comprehends much more easily how to use sacred groves of Verbena in overcoming distances. :-)<br /> Considering the differences in methods, approach and what effects are actually happening...some would say you would have to rebuy the Spheres at full cost.<br /> <br /> A former Technocrat can convert two of his Spheres, while someone who was Verbena from the start will 'only' learn one Sphere with the same time, effort &amp; resources investment. :&gt;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/435410-da-pillars-for-the-modern-day-traditions?p=916086#post916086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's e very good way of illustrating that the older and more powerful mages become &quot;set&quot; in their ways. which is why we'll never ever see voormas becoming an akashic.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Half the listed cost&quot; is considered too high of a rate by him to convert? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/435410-da-pillars-for-the-modern-day-traditions?p=916086#post916086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">think of it like that let's say you can either be a brawler or a martial artist.<br /> you have 1 point in brawl and want to swap;. at that point it;s east<br /> <br /> but ... if you have 5 points in brawl. are you really going to consider it&quot; especially since at that point picking new things is hard for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is different. Brawl and Martial Arts dots don't convert to each other, I think?<br /> <br /> <br /> Nephandi fact: the Nephandi (or at least the Aswadim) also use the Sphere Paradigm, according to <i>The Ascension</i> scenarios book. There is one Aswadim each for Prime, Spirit, Time, Mind, Correspondence and Entropy.<br /> Forces, Life and Matter are considered &quot; (...) <i>too &quot;base and fleeting&quot;</i><i> to be worthy their own exemplars, though all six of the Aswadim are quite proficient in the use of <b>all</b> the Qlippothic Spheres. </i>&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/435410-da-pillars-for-the-modern-day-traditions?p=916086#post916086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the other problem is(At least in my opinion) that the game sort of loses flavour.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that there is more to being a Mage than having the will to learn Spheres within a Paradigm.<br /> A Mage is Awakened, and thus has an Avatar, and an Essence. Note that there are only eight (nine, if you include &quot;The Infinite Essence&quot; mentioned in 1st edition Core) Essences. This suggests that there are certain - solidly defined and limited - number of rules and fundamentals underlying how Awakened Dynamic Magick functions; a relatively (compared to the concept of limitless possibilities) limited amount of stable shapes in regards to how humans interact with the Avatars to weave it.<br /> <br /> Thus, within the rules established by the <i>Mage's</i> background, it <i>can</i> make perfect sense that Correspondence: Data is convertible to mystic take on Correspondence. Cause the NWO Operative was at least skirting the same grounds before he defected to a Tradition. As long as you are Mage working with distances and relations...you are moving within the Sphere of Correspondence (regardless whether the outlook of Sphere of Correspondence is <i>the</i> truth, or not)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 06-17-2016, 05:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T03:23:29-07:00","id":916103,"title":"","content":"uhm 8 essences? don't you mean 4?(unless you count nephandi essences)<br /> <br /> 1) brawl and martial arts don't convert to one another. this was just one(admittedly simplistic) example. my point was le'ts assume for the sake of argument, that in real life you can either be a brawler or a martial artist<br /> <br /> 2) you are right about the nephandi. though this might be a case of gameplay and story segragation. plus al aswad has like what? 59 dots of spheres? my point is that if one mage has a ridiculous numbers of pillars and the other mage has a ridiculous number of spheres they can both do pretty much the same things.<br /> especially since al aswad is an oracle. <br /> <br /> finally the existence of pillars and spheres is not mutually exclusive. for instance in the modern era most mages use the spheres. yet that etruscan lich from dead magic would certainly use the pillars.<br /> <br /> 3)note: the spheres do indeed exist. from a metagame perspective they are indeed &quot;correct&quot; that is, when my hermetic uses primus to summon a spirit he is indeed resonating with the shard realm of spirit. when a syndicate member used primal utility to turn a corporation(or what ever) into quint he is indeed using prime 4 and entropy 5(a corporation is an idea, and money is only useful because people think it is after all)<br /> <br /> <br /> 4)it's just that no paradigm by default(unless youre an oracle i guess like the aforementioned aswadim) incorporates all aspects of all spheres. when every tradition adopted the sphere system they ,in a way circumcised themselves a bit( though it certainly did have it's advantages,this cannot be contested)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T06:01:52-07:00","id":916144,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/435410-da-pillars-for-the-modern-day-traditions?p=916103#post916103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) you are right about the nephandi. though this might be a case of gameplay and story segragation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually thought about this before. The detail with which Al-Aswad, and the other Aswadim, are fleshed out in the <i>&quot;Hell on Earth&quot;</i> scenario would, at first glance, suggest that it's not gameplay and story segregation (that is, that the Aswadim indeed follow the Sphere Paradigm).<br /> However, maybe it is, in a way, gameplay and story segregation. As in, the authors made the Aswadim use the Sphere Paradigm within their background, because there wasn't enough word count to flesh out their unique approaches and Paradigms.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Pillars: <i>Desire | Curiosity | Excess | Avarice</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Excess</i> is keyed to the Sphere of Time primarily, through <i>Desire</i> and <i>Avarice. </i>It is also linked to Spirit through <i>Avarice</i>, Prime through <i>Curiosity</i>, Entropy through <i>Curiosity,</i> and Matter through <i>Desire</i>.<br /> <br /> <i>Curiosity</i> is keyed to the Sphere of Prime primarily, through <i>Desire</i> and <i>Excess. </i>It is also linked to Mind through <i>Avarice</i>, Entropy through <i>Excess, </i>Life through <i>Avarice</i>, and Correspondence through <i>Desire</i>.<br /> <br /> <i>Avari</i>ce is keyed to the Sphere of Mind primarily, through <i>Desire</i> and <i>Curiosity. </i>It is also linked to Time through <i>Excess</i>, Spirit through <i>Excess, </i>Life through <i>Curiosity</i>, and Correspondence through <i>Desire</i>.<br /> <br /> <i>Desire</i> is keyed to the Sphere of Correspondence primarily, through <i>Curiosity</i> and <i>Avarice</i>. It is also linked to Time through <i>Excess, </i>Matter through <i>Excess</i>, Prime through <i>Curiosity</i>, and Mind through <i>Avarice</i>.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, in order to make a point to the Traditions, a True Mage of this Paradigm would say:<br /> \u201cThe Sphere of Correspondence is keyed to <i>Desire, </i>the Sphere of Prime to <i>Curiosity</i>, the Sphere of Time to <i>Excess</i> and the Sphere of Mind \u2013 keyed to <i>Mind</i>.\u201d<br /> <br /> ( I think those pairs work very well on a conceptual and practical level.<br /> You can conjure gifts to someone using <i>Desire</i>, and <i>Avarice Desire:</i> Correspondence and Matterindeed is ideal for putting persons, and spirits, to sleep :-) )<br /> <br /> <br /> How does this work in practice?<br /> For example, followers of this Paradigm can Ward spirits off through use of <i>Excess </i>and <i>Avarice</i>. This results in Wards that work on the principle that \u201cWhy would you bother me in my sanctum, inlaid with gold and jewels, while I'm going through 20 grams of amphetamine?.&quot; Even the most stalwart demonic pursuers pause and apologize, awed by the <i>Excess</i> and the the sheer nonchalance of a Mage's <i>Avarice. </i>Depending how the Mages handles the interaction (remember the demons <i>did</i> intrude upon a Sanctum, so they are in a way, at a disadvantage :-) ) the demons might even promise some way of making up for disrupting the Mage. Do think carefully before offering a line of coke to a demon - it might cause him to become psychotic or paranoid...if the dosage is wrong. :-)<br /> This can work without any spells cast beforehand, or it can involve some kind of ritual can to establish the Wards<br /> <br /> Time effects based on the <i>Excess-Avarice </i>link involve dedication and, sooner or later, sacrifice of precious items and works of art. The <i>Excess-Desire</i> line of Time effects work by trances \u2013 whether reached through tantra or through the use of stimulating substances. (of course, both of those can be used at once in a trance)<br /> <br /> The <i>Avarice</i>-<i>Desire</i> link (which has Correspondence and Mind as it's Spheres) involves astral projection, lucid dreaming (can be used to establish various Mind 1 effects, including Mind Shields) and manipulating other person's dreams - personally, or at a distance.<br /> <br /> Another property of such gifts is that, if someone throws them away...they have a tendency to reappear...<i>Take a long walk up to a river, throw it and run away without turning your back...you come back to your apartment, and the pendant you've accepted is right next to your bed, shining on a table :- ) You could destroy it maybe, but how could you do it, if you didn't do it in the first place?^^</i> This reappearing can be guided dynamically by the Mage, of course.<br /> So when this person who tried to throw away the pendant hears &quot;<i>...but how could you do it, if you didn't do it in the first place?^^</i>&quot; it could very well mean that the pendant is now immune to getting damaged by force...in a way, <i>it's now a better pendant :-)</i> <i>So think carefully, if you'll be planning to melt it using fire. </i>)<br /> <br /> <i>Avarice</i> 3, <i>Desire</i> 2, <i>Curiosity </i>1 could make someone daydream about the Mage or someone or something else. This daydreaming can make someone vulnerable for the <i>Desire </i>4 <i>Avarice </i>2 gift-giving.<br /> <i>( Curiosity</i> is needed to see someone's current state to fullest extent, and direct <i>Desire </i>and <i>Avarice</i> to lull someone into daydreaming state. )<br /> <br /> This Paradigm, as per the dualistic (or contrasting) Foundation, would focus heavily on interactions between two Pillars to achieve it's effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 06-02-2023, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T06:31:37-07:00","id":916150,"title":"","content":"the case with the aswadim is a bit complicated. it doesn't help that the hell on earth scanario... was not exactly the best written.(in fact i think malcolm sheppard stated that in his view this scenario is nothing more than al aswad's personal hell. where he dreams that he is winning)<br /> i think it's more like the oracles choose to not interfere(for instance dante). it's worth noting that the aswadim themselves do not really interfere until the end days. when the time for subtlety is over.<br /> <br /> by the way although nephandi are normally said to follow their old paradigms(inverted of course) i do like yours very well. do you by any chance have the full write up somewhere?<br /> if not can you tell me this: what would these pillars do on their own? after all a beginning nephandi doesn't have the luxury of having at least 2 dots on all of them right?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T08:25:12-07:00","id":916226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/435410-da-pillars-for-the-modern-day-traditions?p=916150#post916150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i think it's more like the oracles choose to not interfere(for instance dante). it's worth noting that the aswadim themselves do not really interfere until the end days. when the time for subtlety is over.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are noted as coming to teach individual Nephandi, without introducing themselves as an Aswad. As well as sometimes saving those Nephandi from difficult situations. That is being present in a situation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/435410-da-pillars-for-the-modern-day-traditions?p=916150#post916150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">by the way although nephandi are normally said to follow their old paradigms(inverted of course) i do like yours very well. do you by any chance have the full write up somewhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is all I have. Though if you want to better envision this, it would be good to draw a square with one of the Pillars in each corner. Then, from the Pillars, draw two lines to each other Pillar. (total of 12 lines) Now fill the lines with the appropriate Spheres which link the Pillars - you can do it as in my previous post, or you can come up with your own. (for example, Life could be linked to Excess somehow)<br /> <br /> I came to this idea today, when I read you refer to \u201cgameplay and story segregation\u201d and thought that yes, the Aswadim (or at least The Harlot Empress, The Aswad of Prime) deserve their own Foundation and Pillars. I plan to work on a complete version of this Paradigm within the next week (hopefully it will be finished by the end of the next month)<br /> <br /> The Hierophant of Winds (the Aswad of Correspondence) also sounds interesting: he is described as walking the paths of Earth, even as he broods in his tower, bearing news and tidings. This to me suggests a take on Correspondence where undergoing the journey, and the journey itself, does matter. A contrast to the &quot;doing away with distances&quot; focus on Correspondence that I've seen so far to be prevalent in Mage.<br /> I'm imagining how, depending which turn he takes at a crossroads, different things happen to different people, at different places and in different situations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/435410-da-pillars-for-the-modern-day-traditions?p=916150#post916150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if not can you tell me this: what would these pillars do on their own? after all a beginning nephandi doesn't have the luxury of having at least 2 dots on all of them right?</div> </div> </div> </div>They wouldn't need two dots in each of them if we assume all effects would take at least two Pillars. They would need two dots spread between at least two of them to achieve some amount of effects. Not much, granted \u2013 but this is so with every young Mage.<br /> <br /> But as I envision it, the Pillars could be used on their own. For now I'm thinking the below. ( This is subject to change...right now I'm finding it very hard to envision just how to divide all the effects per those concepts..but I'm sure it can be done, and that I can do it with time :P :-) Anyone else is welcome to try, as well.<br /> <br /> <i>Desire \u2013</i> reading auras and moods, pro-active divination, scrying, divining the future<br /> Influencing minds when charming someone.<br /> Relations Sense / Sight - can be used on items, people, places....Can be used to ascertain how strong of a link an item or a person will provide to someone.<br /> <br /> <i>Curiosity</i> \u2013 Life, Entropy and Prime sight(s) &amp; senses<br /> Putting humans to sleep :-).<br /> Putting spirits to sleep (with added Excess or Avarice) :-).<br /> Hostile (or at least hostile at first glance) curses<br /> General and various energy manipulation and redirection within another person, group or a location.<br /> <br /> <i>Excess \u2013 </i>Perfect Timing, charming spirits<br /> Multiplication of wealth - the definition of wealth matters here a lot; it might be a Matter effect, or it might be something different...someone could also be cursed with an excess of something, especially if they wished for it ;-)<br /> While in Sanctum: prolonging time periods by whole hours (so a night lasting 20-25 hours is doable for an Arete 5+)<br /> Value &amp; Worth Sense / Sight \u2013 this would be in regards to seeing how much items (including magic items) are worth. Either in cash or in any other currency. Trying to ascertain the value priceless items \u2013 like a photo of a loved one or an engagement ring (or a pair of such rings) \u2013 is Paradox prone, but can produce great and interesting results.<br /> Periapt creation.<br /> <br /> <i>Avarice</i> \u2013 influencing minds, minds shields, catalyzing one's mind processes, Time Sense, passive divination (for example knowing if somebody is plotting against you), divining the past<br /> Channeling &amp; gifting Quintessence, or other kinds of energy, to other people or spirits.<br /> Making health recovery faster.<br /> <br /> <i>Perceptions</i>, <i>experiences,</i> and <i>reflecting </i>(in thought, attitude, and action) on both of them them is important within this Paradigm.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Spheres Keyed and linked to each Pillar can be written up as different. I was just thinking: <i>Desire</i> keyed to Time, Curiosity keyed to Entropy, <i>Excess </i>keyed to Prime, and <i>Avarice </i>remaining keyed to Mind. Entropy replaces Correspondence in one of the <i>Curiosity-Desire</i> links. Correspondence remains within the <i>Desire-Avarice</i> link.<br /> <br /> <b><i><u>Edit:</u> </i></b>If anyone is wondering about how I'd envision The Harlot Empress, The Aswad of Prime, within this Paradigm...She has the Foundation at a 9 and the Pillars at: <i>Desire</i> 9 | <i>Curiosity</i> 8 | <i>Excess</i> 7 | <i>Avarice </i>7<br /> &quot;<i>The Harlot Empress disdains clothing entirely, using desire as her first and foremost magic and thereby ensnaring all those who look upon her in webs spun of their own lusts.</i>&quot;<br /> &quot;<i>She has a ripe, voluptuous body and the face of a goddess.</i>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 02-19-2018, 03:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T08:54:31-07:00","id":918645,"title":"","content":"Maybe the Disparate Alliance and crafts could use their own pillars. <br /> <br /> For me the matter is about a character from Dark Age with pillars who become memeber of the nine traditions and then starts to learn spheres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T10:55:40-07:00","id":918699,"title":"","content":"IMHO, it should be easier to switch from a Foundation to Arete than it is to switch from one Foundation to another or from Arete to a Foundation. Reason? Foundations and their Pillars are intimately tied to specific practices, as evidenced by the fact that each published Pillar has a set of instruments associated with it. Switching from Foundation to Arete would let you keep your practice and its instruments, resulting in a much smaller barrier to learning. (Actually, Arete to Foundation <i>can</i> be as easy as going from Foundation to Arete, but only if the Traditionist's practice matches the Foundation's practice.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-19-2019, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T09:11:30-07:00","id":919123,"title":"","content":"Foundation &gt; Arete and vice-versa is easier to encompass than the attendant Pillar &gt; Sphere issue. The powers of a Pillar could be distributed over several different Spheres at various levels of power. Plus the Arete as a hard limit on Sphere access would be an issue as well. There are others far better equipped than I to go into the particulars of how that would look, but it would be very... interesting. <br /> <br /> The Foundation/Pillar user would definitely see some weird losses in their &quot;power suite&quot; and, probably, those new positiveness that would accrue wouldn't seem like adequate recompense. Especially since some of those new possibilities might not even be readily/easily accessible due the limitations imposed by Focus and praxis/paradigm. <br /> <br /> Then again, there are definitely some fluff precedents for such. &quot;Magic changes over time&quot; and all Something akin to that is what seems to have set Tremere off on his massive misadventure...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T10:49:38-07:00","id":1298003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/435410-da-pillars-for-the-modern-day-traditions?p=435874#post435874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was a thread a bit ago about redesigning the Spheres. My idea was to basically add in 3 sub-Sphere level traits per Sphere (Ok it was bigger than that, but it's the part that matters to this) that allowed a bit more flavor/customization. The point of this was to keep the general Sphere structure and the cross-compatibility stuff, but have more Tradition/Splat flavor around. So a Verbena and an Etherite might have the same dots in Life, but the Verbena might have &quot;Healing, Shapeshifting, and Plant Mastery,&quot; to reflect how they relate to Life and what kind of spells they're good at, while the Etherite might have, &quot;Body Modification, Genetics, and Homeostatic Control.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> I guess some of this is rather than looking at &quot;limiting&quot; mages into their Tradition/Splat paradigms, doing more of a carrot to encourage them to play to the strengths of their paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps each player should have 2 or 3 'specialties' that a player needs to choose that get reduced difficulties. This would entice players to cast those spells in times of difficulty to get the best chance of success. If I were a wizard in stress, a situation where things were getting very difficult, I would naturally fall back on my strengths and fundamentals without even thinking about it.<br /> <br /> Lower difficulties for certain sub-spheres or specialties would give players incentive to cast along those lines. Thus, creating a flavor of a character that differs from another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13189-knowledgeseeker","name":"Knowledgeseeker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}